  <content>
  <section><title>Writing Equivalent Linear Forms</title>
<para>Write an equation of a line in all three forms that has a slope of 2 and a \(y\)-intercept of 7.</para>
<para><emphasis>Slope-Intercept Form</emphasis></para>
<para><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></para>
<para>Remember that \(A\) can not be negative and there should not be any fractions or decimals.</para>
<para>For this form, rearrange slope-intercept form to lead with the \(x\) term:</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Bring the \(x\) and \(y\) terms on the left side.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Simplify.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Divide all terms by -1 so that \(A\) is not negative.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Simplify.</para>
<para><emphasis>Point-Slope Form</emphasis></para>
<para>Notice this can easily be written in slope-intercept form by solving for \(y\):</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-7&amp;=&amp;2(x-0)\\y-7&amp;=&amp;2x-0\\y-7+7&amp;=&amp;2x-0+7\\y&amp;=&amp;2x+7\end{array}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Standard Form to Slope-Intercept Form</emphasis></para>
<para>Write \(3x - 5y = 14\) in slope-intercept form.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Bring the \(x\) term to the right side with the constant.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Simplify.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Divide by the coefficient of \(y\). </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Simplify and write in the correct order.</para>
<title>Try It: Writing Equivalent Linear Forms</title>
<!--Q#-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write the equation \(3x +8y =24\) in slope-intercept form.</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: \(y=-\frac{3x}{8}+3\)</para>
    <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}3x-3x +8y &amp;=&amp;24-3x \\8y &amp;=&amp;24-3x\\\frac{8y}{8} &amp;=&amp;\frac{24}{8}-\frac{3x}{8}\\y&amp;=&amp;-\frac{3x}{8}+3\end{array}\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
